ocation":"1.44 SW Mt Gilead Arpt","lon":-82.8722,"magnitude":55.0,"magnitudeType":"EG","narrative":"Trees downed along U.S. Route 42, just east of Burr Road, on the northeast side of Cardington.","source":"Trained Spotter","state":"OH","type":"Thunderstorm Wind","wfo":"CLE"},{"begin":"2026-03-27T00:42Z","county":"Morrow","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2026-03-27T00:42Z","endLat":40.6714,"endLon":-82.8403,"episode":211146,"id":1324968,"injuries":0,"lat":40.6714,"location":"0.52 E Iberia","lon":-82.8403,"magnitude":0.88,"narrative":"Hail up to nickel-size in Iberia.","source":"Trained Spotter","state":"OH","type":"Hail","wfo":"CLE"},{"begin":"2026-03-27T00:43Z","county":"Morrow","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"35.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2026-03-27T00:45Z","endLat":40.5423,"endLon":-82.7876,"episode":211146,"id":1319117,"injuries":0,"lat":40.5586,"location":"1.33 ENE Mt Gilead","lon":-82.8073,"narrative":"This tornado had peak intensity of EF1, with estimated peak winds of 95-mph, and impacted the northeastern and eastern outskirts of Mount Gilead. The tornado began along U.S. Route 42, near Home Road, and caused extensive tree damage, which included multiple snapped and uprooted trees. The tornado continued southeastward, crossed Township Road 103, and caused sporadic tree damage. The tornado then crossed OH Route 95, near Township Road 110, and destroyed a 60 foot by 100 foot outbuilding. Debris from this outbuilding were displaced about 100 to 200 yards to the south-southeast by the tornado before the tornado ended. Scattered tree damage and some structural damage associated with straight line convective wind gusts up to 75-mph were found both north and south of the tornado track. Radar data suggest this tornado was associated with a cyclonic mesovortex along the poleward side of the descending rear-inflow jet of a bow echo and the bow echo was embedded within the flanking line of a cyclonic supercell.","source":"NWS Storm Su