:-83.6109,"narrative":"The first tornadic damage was observed at the Hardin County Fairgrounds, just south of County Road 140, where minor roof damage occurred. Several wooden power poles were damaged and snapped in half. On the northern side of the fairgrounds, a hardwood tree was snapped and a building sustained a major loss of its metal roofing panels. An additional building had its concrete block siding blown out, which caused a partial roof collapse. An open-ended barn structure was lifted, causing the support poles to be lifted and shifted. The final damage associated with this tornado was on the eastern side of the fairgrounds, where additional power poles were snapped and minor roof damage was observed to fairground buildings.","source":"NWS Storm Survey","state":"OH","torLengthMi":0.13,"torScale":"EF1","torWidthYd":75.0,"type":"Tornado","wfo":"ILN"},{"begin":"2026-03-27T00:46Z","county":"Morrow","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"8.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2026-03-27T00:46Z","endLat":40.5483,"endLon":-82.7636,"episode":211146,"id":1325021,"injuries":0,"lat":40.5483,"location":"2.61 WNW Pulaskiville","lon":-82.7636,"magnitude":65.0,"magnitudeType":"EG","narrative":"Roof damaged at Hidden Lakes and numerous trees downed at and near Hidden Lakes.","source":"Broadcast Media","state":"OH","type":"Thunderstorm Wind","wfo":"CLE"},{"begin":"2026-03-27T00:47Z","county":"Morrow","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2026-03-27T00:47Z","endLat":40.5989,"endLon":-82.7477,"episode":211146,"id":1324996,"injuries":0,"lat":40.5989,"location":"1.6 NW Williamsport","lon":-82.7477,"magnitude":1.5,"narrative":"Hail up to ping pong ball-size about two-miles northwest of Williamsport.","source":"Public","state":"OH","type":"Hail","wfo":"CLE"},{"begin":"2026-03-27T00:49Z","county":"Morrow","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2026-03-27T00:49Z","endLat":40.5299,"endLon":-82.7015,"episode":211146,"id":1325016,"injuries":0,"