9 NE Macksburg","lon":-81.4636,"narrative":"Duck Creek at Macksburg rose above a bankfull level of 13 feet on the morning of March 27th, then continued to rise to a crest around 14 feet that night. The creek then receded back below bankfull level early the next morning. Impacts in the midst of the creek spilling out of its banks included flooding of Main Street, and fields and low-lying areas adjacent to the creek.","source":"River/Stream Gage","state":"OH","type":"Flood","wfo":"RLX"},{"begin":"2026-03-27T16:43Z","county":"Washington","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2026-03-28T03:52Z","endLat":39.5446,"endLon":-81.247,"episode":210769,"id":1320044,"injuries":0,"lat":39.5687,"location":"0.35 WSW Bloomfield","lon":-81.2063,"narrative":"The Little Muskingum at Bloomfield rose above a bankfull level of 16 feet shortly near mid day on March 27th, then continued to rise to a crest around 18.5 feet late that afternoon. The river then receded back below bankfull level that night. Portions of State Route 26 between Hills Bridge Road and Griffin Hill Road were closed due to flooding as a result.","source":"River/Stream Gage","state":"OH","type":"Flood","wfo":"RLX"},{"begin":"2026-03-27T20:16Z","county":"Athens","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2026-03-27T23:16Z","endLat":39.4909,"endLon":-82.085,"episode":210769,"id":1320047,"injuries":0,"lat":39.5,"location":"0.28 W Glouster","lon":-82.0853,"narrative":"Sunday Creek began to flood adjacent roads, including Kennedy Road near Trimble High School.","source":"Trained Spotter","state":"OH","type":"Flood","wfo":"RLX"}]}